{"name":"Spinel Black","hex":"#464d4a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spinel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several hard minerals of cubic symmetry that are mixed oxides of magnesium and aluminium and are used as gemstones of various colours.","Any crystalline material, not necessarily an oxide, that possesses the same crystal structure as this mineral."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Spindle; the amount of yarn that fits on a spindle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinel"},{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinel","blocks":[{"text":"Spinel is the magnesium/aluminium member of the larger spinel group of minerals. It has the formula MgAl2O4 in the cubic crystal system. The name comes from the Latin word spinella, a diminutive form of spine, in reference to its pointed crystals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Calcite-Spinel-dtn37a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinel","wikidata":"Q191310"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/MgAl2O4.png/500px-MgAl2O4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/MgAl2O4.png/1280px-MgAl2O4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/MgAl2O4.png/500px-MgAl2O4.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polyhedral representation of spinel MgAl2O4","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMgAl2O4.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg/500px-Mus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg/1280px-Mus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg/500px-Mus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Synthetic spinel made using the hydrothermal method","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMus%C3%A9um_de_Nantes_-_011_-_Spinelle_synth%C3%A9tique_hydrothermal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wiki